In October 2024, the Division of Drinking Water (DDW) surveyed 34 laboratories accredited by DDW's Environmental Laboratory Accreditation Program (ELAP) for EPA Method 533 and/or EPA Method 537.1. Each laboratory was asked to identify the following:
- Capability: Minimum reporting level (MRL) for 7 different PFAS, including ability to detect at U.S. EPA's Practical Quantitation Levels (PQLs)
- Capacity: Number of analyses able to be performed per month;
- Cost: Cost per analysis;
- And more.
20 laboratories responded to the survey: 14 commercial laboratories and 6 municipal laboratories. Of the responding laboratories: 17 laboratories were accredited for both EPA Method 533 and EPA Method 537.1, 2 laboratories were accredited for EPA Method 533, and 1 laboratory was accredited for EPA Method 537.1. Survey responses are summarized below:

