• At least 6 to 15 sampling points (wells) must be available for spatial analysis;
• Monitoring data must have the appropriate quality for comparability (same analytical methods, detection limits, sampling methods etc.).
Total Cost of LTMO
The total cost of a site’s LTMO is the sum of the cost of the LTMO study and the cost of implementing the study’s recommendations. LTMO study implementation costs may consist of:
• Costs related to obtaining stakeholders buy-in, including regulatory approval of new/updated GMP;
• Potential installation/replacement of wells (could be deferred if no funding is available).
