• Surface cover at site (asphalt, concrete, soil, grass);
• Building ventilation properties that may affect convection of soil gas into the structure (e.g., positively pressurized building, ventilation air-exchange rate), and mixing in the building; and • Corrective measures in place that may limit migration of constituents into the building (e.g., source remediation, mitigation measures such as a vapor barrier).
